{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q417652","formula":"FHO","hill":"FHO","elements":["H","O","F"],"composition":{"F":1.0,"H":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Hypofluorous acid","ru":"Фторноватистая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hypofluorous acid, chemical formula HOF, is the only known oxyacid of fluorine and the only known oxoacid in which the main atom gains electrons from oxygen to create a negative oxidation state. The oxidation state of the oxygen in this acid (and in the hypofluorite ion OF− and in its salts called hypofluorites) is 0, while its valence is 2. It is also the only hypohalous acid that can be isolated as a solid.","ru":"Фторнова́тистая кислота́ (фтороксигенат(0) водорода) — неорганическое соединение водорода, кислорода и фтора с формулой HOF, в котором формальная степень окисления кислорода равна 0. Название получила по аналогии с хлорноватистой кислотой HOCl. Кислотных свойств не проявляет, солей не образует, однако существуют ковалентные производные формального замещения водорода, называемые гипофторитами."},"fame":31,"pubchemCid":123334,"mass":36.006,"charge":0,"smiles":"OF","inchikey":"AQYSYJUIMQTRMV-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"hypofluorous acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"123334","atoms":3,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.705,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"F"},{"x":0.705,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":1.044,"y":0.656,"z":-0.632,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[1,2,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417652","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypofluorous_acid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A4%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%82%D